<task id="AIR2-020" project="spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Triple-twin validator hoist — single authored catalog source → generated/validated mirrors [FR-A-01]</title>
    <status>completed</status>
    <phase>A-infra — before ANY catalog-row task</phase>
    <gate>G-R2-A (enabling infra)</gate>
    <estimated-effort>2-3 days</estimated-effort>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Source-of-truth migration for catalog guidance/contract text with high blast radius — it BLOCKS every catalog-row task in three r2 waves (032/042/057). A wrong single-source shape or a validator that under-enforces parity silently ships drift into all three surfaces. Architectural, cross-cutting, hard to reverse.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <goal-eligible>false</goal-eligible>
    <tags>bff-api, catalog-governance, adr-039, validator, blocking-infra</tags>
    <dependencies>none (front-loaded; MUST merge before 032/042/057 and any memory.* row)</dependencies>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Hoist the guidance/contract text that today lives in THREE hand-maintained twins — the live catalog `sprk_description` in Dataverse, the handler `Metadata` description in code, and the `infra/dataverse/inputschemas/` seed mirror — to ONE authored source with generated/validated mirrors, and extend `OpenAiFunctionSchemaValidator` + `RoutingConsumerTypeHealthCheck` to enforce parity across all three (spec FR-A-01 / R15, plan §4 Phase A-infra). This BLOCKS all catalog-row tasks: r2 adds rows in ≥3 core waves (Policy v2 risk-factor fields at 032, create-matter at 042, `memory.write` at 057), and every one of them must be authored THROUGH this hoisted source. The `memory.*` rows are the first consumers.
  </prompt>

  <role>Senior .NET developer fluent in the ADR-039 closed-catalog model, the JPS input-schema pipeline (`jps-action-create`/`jps-validate`), and Dataverse seed-mirror generation.</role>

  <goal>
    A single authored catalog-guidance source exists; the live `sprk_description`, the handler `Metadata` description, and the `infra/dataverse/inputschemas/` seed mirror are all generated/validated FROM it (not hand-edited independently). `OpenAiFunctionSchemaValidator` (Services/Ai/Chat/OpenAiFunctionSchemaValidator.cs:70) and `RoutingConsumerTypeHealthCheck` (Services/Ai/PublicContracts/RoutingConsumerTypeHealthCheck.cs:66) are extended to FAIL when any of the three surfaces drifts from the authored source. A single-source edit propagates to all three with validator-enforced parity, proven end-to-end by authoring the `memory.*` rows through it. No catalog row can be added except through the hoisted source thereafter.
  </goal>

  <inputs>
    <file purpose="spec">projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r2/spec.md</file>
    <file purpose="plan">projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r2/plan.md</file>
    <file purpose="design">projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r2/design.md</file>
    <file purpose="module-guidance">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/CLAUDE.md</file>
    <file purpose="bff-governance">.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
    <file purpose="discovery">projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r2/notes/ (FR-P0-04 validator-extension-point discovery note)</file>
  </inputs>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-039">Closed catalogs, one intent mechanism — the hoist reshapes WHERE catalog text is authored, never adds a second intent/dispatch mechanism. Risk factors stay catalog-declared DATA.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">Any facade text consumed by CRUD stays reachable only via `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Parity enforcement is exercised by a KEEP-path test that authors a row through the source and asserts three-surface propagation; no `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, no DI-registration tests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-032">If parity enforcement is feature-gated during rollout, the gate uses a Null-Object kill-switch — no asymmetric registration.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">MUST sequence BEFORE 032, 042, 057, and any `memory.*` catalog-row task (spec MUST rule). This task's own PR merges first.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Additive-only to the authoring format; existing rows migrate via a tolerant generator, not a hand rewrite of all rows.</constraint>
    <constraint source="bff-hygiene">Run the bff-extensions.md checklist; state Placement Justification; measure publish-size delta vs the ~49.63 MB (incl. PDBs) baseline; no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>ai/closed-catalog, catalog-governance, input-schema-mirrors, health-check-parity</topic>
    <files>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-039-grounded-execution-closed-catalogs.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-013-*.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Function-schema validator" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Chat/OpenAiFunctionSchemaValidator.cs">Line 70 — the validation entry point to EXTEND with three-surface parity enforcement.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Routing-consumer health check" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/RoutingConsumerTypeHealthCheck.cs">Line 66 — startup/health parity assertion surface; add the authored-source-vs-mirror drift check here.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Seed mirror home" location="infra/dataverse/sprk_analysistool-*-row.json">CORRECTED surface (was mis-cited as `infra/dataverse/inputschemas/`, which mirrors a DIFFERENT column `sprk_analysisaction.sprk_inputschema`, not the tool-description prose). The genuine third description twin is the `sprk_analysistool-*-row.json` seed rows carrying `sprk_description` — confirmed by r1 UAT note g-p3-uat-round4-findings.md:274-280. These row files are the SINGLE AUTHORED SOURCE (Model 1 / GitOps); live `sprk_description` is a seed-managed mirror; handler `Metadata.Description` is a code mirror validated in CI.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <context>
    <background>R1 P4 left three hand-maintained copies of each capability's guidance/contract text; they drift silently. r2 adds rows in three waves, so the drift surface grows unless authoring is single-sourced FIRST. This is design §10 row 15 and the load-bearing enabler for Policy v2's catalog-declared risk factors.</background>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="none" status="n/a">Front A-infra task — no upstream.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
    <related-work>
      <item>032 (Policy v2) authors the reversibility/external-visibility/deadline/confidentiality/record-of-truth risk-factor fields THROUGH this source — its catalog changes sequence behind this hoist.</item>
      <item>042 (create-matter) and 057 (`memory.write`) are downstream catalog-row consumers.</item>
      <item>FR-P0-04 discovery note confirmed the validator extension points before this task.</item>
    </related-work>
  </context>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="0" name="Context + governance">Load FR-A-01, ADR-039, the FR-P0-04 discovery note, bff-extensions.md. Confirm the exact validator entry point (OpenAiFunctionSchemaValidator.cs:70) and health-check surface (RoutingConsumerTypeHealthCheck.cs:66).</step>
    <step order="1" name="Design the authored source">Define the single-source format (one authored record per capability holding the guidance/contract text + the risk-factor property slots Policy v2 will populate). Decide file-vs-Dataverse home for the authored source; document the choice + rationale.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Generators">Write the generator that emits the three mirrors FROM the authored source: (a) live `sprk_description` payload, (b) handler `Metadata` description, (c) `infra/dataverse/inputschemas/*.input.schema.json`. Generation is deterministic (stable ordering; no timestamps).</step>
    <step order="3" name="Validator + health-check extension">Extend `OpenAiFunctionSchemaValidator` (:70) to fail when a handler `Metadata` description diverges from the authored source; extend `RoutingConsumerTypeHealthCheck` (:66) to fail on seed-mirror / live-description drift. Parity failure is a hard fail, not a warning.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Migrate existing rows">Run the generator across existing rows via the tolerant generator (additive-only); confirm zero behavioral change to existing capabilities (byte-diff mirrors where possible).</step>
    <step order="5" name="Prove with memory.* rows">Author the `memory.*` rows through the single source and assert propagation to all three surfaces + validator-green — this is the acceptance proof, not a paper claim.</step>
    <step order="6" name="Contract/parity test">Add a KEEP-path test: edit the source for one row → assert all three surfaces change + validator passes; corrupt one mirror out-of-band → assert the validator/health-check FAILS.</step>
    <step order="7" name="Verify + governance">Build; run the test; measure publish-size delta; state Placement Justification + bff-extensions checklist in PR notes.</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build + run the parity/contract test</tool>
    <tool name="jps-validate">Validate generated input-schema mirrors</tool>
    <tool name="git">Commit on the project branch</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/ (single authored-source model + generator)</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Chat/OpenAiFunctionSchemaValidator.cs (parity enforcement)</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/RoutingConsumerTypeHealthCheck.cs (drift check)</output>
    <output type="code">infra/dataverse/inputschemas/ (now GENERATED mirrors)</output>
    <output type="test">tests/ (single-source-edit → three-surface propagation; corrupt-mirror → validator fails)</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r2/notes/ (authoring format + generator + rollout doc)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A single authored source exists; the live `sprk_description`, handler `Metadata` description, and `infra/dataverse/inputschemas/` mirror are all generated/validated FROM it — none is hand-edited independently.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A single-source edit for one capability propagates to all three surfaces (asserted by test); validator + health-check pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`OpenAiFunctionSchemaValidator` (:70) and `RoutingConsumerTypeHealthCheck` (:66) are extended to enforce three-surface parity as a HARD fail.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The `memory.*` rows are authored through the single source and propagate correctly — proven, not asserted on paper.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Existing rows migrate with zero behavioral change (mirror diff confirms).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE: corrupting exactly one of the three mirrors out-of-band (so it diverges from the authored source) makes the validator/health-check FAIL — proven by a test.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish-size delta measured + reported; no new HIGH CVE; Placement Justification stated.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">On completion, flip this seam's row in `projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r2/notes/SEAM-STATUS.md` to published (with commit ref); record which Compose r2 FR it unblocks (FR-12). 'Published' = merged + contract test green + consumable via Services/Ai/PublicContracts/.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If any capability's three surfaces cannot be reconciled to a single authored source without changing runtime behavior (i.e., the twins already disagree semantically, not just cosmetically), STOP and surface the divergence per CLAUDE.md §6.5 — the migration must not silently pick a winner that alters a shipped capability's contract.</trigger>
    <trigger>If single-sourcing would require a second authoring/dispatch mechanism to satisfy a row (ADR-039 one-intent tension), surface it rather than forking authoring.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <notes>
    COMPLETED 2026-07-08 (Model 1 / GitOps + Option C validate-only, operator-ratified after task-020 escalation).

    SURFACE CORRECTION (project-scoped, per operator instruction 4): the prescribed third twin `infra/dataverse/inputschemas/` was mis-cited — discovery proved it mirrors a DIFFERENT column (`sprk_analysisaction.sprk_inputschema`, input schema of a different entity), not the tool-description prose. The genuine third description twin is `infra/dataverse/sprk_analysistool-*-row.json` (`sprk_description`), confirmed by r1 UAT note g-p3-uat-round4-findings.md:274-280. `inputschemas/` and the Binding-intent surface (`sprk_playbookconsumer.sprk_tooldescription`) are OUT of this hoist. Full discovery + drift census (36 pairs, 0 semantic) in notes/task-020-triple-twin-hoist-design-and-escalation.md.

    IMPLEMENTED:
    - Authored source = `infra/dataverse/sprk_analysistool-*-row.json` `sprk_description` (Model 1). Live `sprk_analysistool.sprk_description` = seed-managed mirror (Seed-TypedHandlers.ps1 PATCHes it; documented seed-managed + do-not-edit-live). Handler `Metadata.Description` = code mirror, reconciled byte-equal for all 23 single-row handlers (Option C, no codegen).
    - Parity mechanism: pure `OpenAiFunctionSchemaValidator.FindDescriptionParityError(authored, mirror)` (NFR-07-safe — lengths + first-diff index only), reused by BOTH enforcement points.
    - CI enforcement: tests/integration/contract/Catalog/CatalogToolDescriptionParityContractTests.cs (KEEP-path; data-driven over the authored rows; positive all-single-row parity + NEGATIVE corrupt-mirror + single-source-edit-propagation + memory.* authored-through-source proof; multi-row + no-row handlers exempt).
    - Runtime enforcement: RoutingConsumerTypeHealthCheck description-parity dimension → Unhealthy when a live single-row sprk_description diverges from the compiled mirror (surfaces a hand-edit the seed would revert). +2 health-check tests.
    - Docs: seed-managed note in Seed-TypedHandlers.ps1 header + ToolHandlerToAIFunctionAdapter projection site. Form-level read-only for sprk_description noted as a follow-up (health-check + seed-revert are the interim enforcement).

    memory.* (task 057) authors THROUGH this source; live seeding deferred to 057 (seeding a row without its handler now would trip the existing bijection health check). Compose's 5 rows author the same way.

    VERIFICATION: BFF build 0 errors; BFF unit suite 7581/7682 (101 skipped; 1 pre-existing flake AuditLogServiceTests.LogInteractionAsync_PartitionsByTenantId — passes in isolation, orthogonal); golden-utterance eval 35/35 green.
  </notes>
</task>
